  "label": "The text 'nuns don't randomly explode' is mapped onto the visual entity of the Muslim woman wearing a hijab.",
  "description": "The meme uses the text 'nuns don't randomly explode' to create an analogical mapping where the Muslim woman in the hijab is implicitly equated with an explosive device. This mapping is part of a harmful stereotype that weaponizes the hijab by associating it with violence or terrorism, while contrasting it with the nun's habit, which is not similarly judged. The text explicitly refers to the second visual entity (the Muslim woman) as if she were an explosive, creating a direct and offensive analogical link between the textual metaphor and the visual representation.",
